keel-overlay-installer (0.2.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * etckeeper does not commit private keys and secrets into /etc/.git
    (Keel-Linux/common#49). Seen on real nodes with keel 0.23.3:
    wireguard/wg0.key at the keel installation and
    mysql/keel-tls/server.key at a reinstallation.
  * The postinst runs /usr/lib/keel/overlays/installer/etckeeper-ignore at
    each configure. It writes this list into /etc/.gitignore, outside the
    section etckeeper manages, so etckeeper's init, update-ignore and
    uninit keep it: wireguard/*.key, mysql/keel-tls/*.key,
    etcd/keel/*.key, keel/secrets/, ssl/private/, ssh/ssh_host_*_key,
    crowdsec/local_api_credentials.yaml,
    crowdsec/online_api_credentials.yaml, crowdsec/bouncers/*.yaml.local,
    anubis/keel.key and anubis/keel.key.*.
  * Where /etc/.git exists, it removes the tracked files of the list from
    the index (git rm --cached) and commits that removal with the new
    .gitignore, and with no other change. The files stay on disk. The
    history is not rewritten.
  * Rotate every key that was tracked: the old commits of /etc/.git still
    hold it, and so does each copy or backup of /etc/.git. The postinst
    lists the files it removed from the index. keel 0.23.3 has no command
    that rotates a key: keel makes each key once, and a renewal of a
    certificate (etcd, the database's TLS) keeps the same key. Rotate the
    SSH host keys, the TLS keys of ssl/private, CrowdSec's credentials and
    Anubis's signing key with the tools of their own packages.

 -- KeelLinux maintainers <admin@keellinux.org>  Fri, 09 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000

keel-overlay-installer (0.1.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * First release (handbook decision 0041, first implementation, step 2).
    Depends on Keel's inithooks 2.3.6+keel14, confconsole 2.2.3+keel8 and
    keel 0.12.0, the first keel that reads manifest_version 1; ships the
    overlay manifest of docs/manifest-v1.md as
    /usr/share/keel/overlays/installer.yaml, whose first boot hooks
    00declarative, 75keel-role and 80keel-cloud are inithooks' and
    10keel-system is keel's.

 -- Marcos Mendez <mendez.foto@gmail.com>  Wed, 30 Sep 2026 15:00:00 +0000
